- # The launch-only (LTI 1.1 "companion mode") variant of the instructor status
- # view. Under 1.1 there is no roster service, no line-item service and no grade
- # passback, so the roster row, the sync rows, the grade-sync trigger and the
- # import/publish next steps of instructor_status have nothing behind them and
- # are left out rather than rendered as permanently "not yet synced". What is
- # left is what a 1.1 course can show: the link confirmation and how many
- # students have connected a Wikipedia account — under 1.1 a student launching
- # and connecting is the only way in, and there is no roster to count them
- # against, which is why the roster-sounding count is gone too. No next-step
- # guidance either: once linked, a 1.1 course has no further setup step, and
- # what the mode does and doesn't do is install-time knowledge (the guide),
- # not something to repeat on every launch.
.lti-iframe__drilldown
  = render 'lti_launch/drilldown_header',
           title: t('lti.status.header'), course: @binding.course, linked_check: true
  %dl.lti-status-list
    .lti-status-list__row
      %dt= t('lms_integration.connected_accounts')
      %dd
        = @sync_status.connected_accounts_count
        - # Re-requests the launch URL inside the iframe only (an in-iframe
        - # anchor never navigates the Canvas page); the count is the one number
        - # here that changes as students connect.
        = link_to t('lti.status.refresh'),
                  "/lti?ltik=#{CGI.escape(params[:ltik].to_s)}",
                  class: 'lti-status-list__refresh'
